{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1502968-assassins-party-make-up","id":1502968,"title":"[Assassins] Party Make Up","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-13T16:12:36-08:00","id":1502968,"title":"[Assassins] Party Make Up","content":"I'm curious to hear what kinds of Assassins games you all are running. I feel like more than most TC games the core concept of Assassins really lends itself to a central character surrounded by a supporting cast. For many tables that concept would be a non-starter. So far I have run a game with mostly Talents and a single Assassin in the mix, and another with only 2 players, but both were Assassins. Even in that second one there was a clear &quot;main character,&quot; because it was a flashback one-shot story designed to flesh out the background of one of the character.<br /> <br /> How are you all structuring your Assassins games? I could imagine a sandbox style game set in a single city where the players all play members of the various Assassin societyies while helping and hindering eachother complete jobs, but I'm not sure that would run very well with my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T20:38:18-07:00","id":1507360,"title":"","content":"The players in my group are all playing Assassins. One is close combat expert, One is a pistol/gun fu guy, one is a saboteur, and one is a sniper. All of them are Daughters of Jacobian and stationed in South America.<br /> <br /> My game has been completely episodic. Currently I'm telling a story set in the background of the Galatea disaster which will eventually lead to them being sent to eliminate an Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T19:52:35-07:00","id":1507451,"title":"","content":"Are your players' working as an established team, or are they simply all members of the same organization and helping eachother out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T00:35:16-07:00","id":1507458,"title":"","content":"My Signal Society team started as one character messeged on... Signal Communicator ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) problem in Hongkong, asking for help on subject and meeting. They then evoluated as playeress personal strike team, when her personal story entwined with their personal mini-war with Swarm.<br /> <br /> We have in team:<ul><li>Mouth - ex-sex worker, now street detective, helping mainly women in need</li> <li>Gunslinger - ex-special forces combat shooter</li> <li>Poisoner - ex-forensic technician, on the look out from Transcendent Alliance</li> </ul>We had also Hacker from Krugu Vorvo, but he step down from personal issues.","signature":"","edit